1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,221
I told the sailors to throw me into the sea

2
00:00:02,241 --> 00:00:04,862
and a great fish swallowed me whole, and

3
00:00:04,922 --> 00:00:06,282
buried me alive in the dark.

4
00:00:07,423 --> 00:00:09,963
I ran from God because His mercy was too wide.

5
00:00:10,784 --> 00:00:13,425
He sent me to Nineveh, the city I hated. I'd

6
00:00:13,465 --> 00:00:15,125
sooner drown than see her spared.

7
00:00:16,146 --> 00:00:18,727
The storm came for my sake; the lot fell on

8
00:00:18,767 --> 00:00:19,067
me.

9
00:00:19,847 --> 00:00:22,128
To spare the sailors, I had them throw me overboard.

10
00:00:22,948 --> 00:00:24,789
Three days buried alive in the fish.

11
00:00:25,509 --> 00:00:28,730
Then, long after I was dust, scribes demanded

12
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:32,171
a sign, Jesus gave them only my name: For

13
00:00:32,231 --> 00:00:34,492
as Jonas was three days and three nights in

14
00:00:34,512 --> 00:00:37,493
the whale's belly; so shall the Son of man

15
00:00:37,613 --> 00:00:40,654
be three days and three nights in the heart

16
00:00:40,974 --> 00:00:41,575
of the earth.

17
00:00:42,235 --> 00:00:44,576
I went down guilty, the storm was mine.

18
00:00:45,276 --> 00:00:47,677
He went down innocent, bearing what was ours;

19
00:00:48,337 --> 00:00:49,157
He gave Himself.

20
00:00:49,757 --> 00:00:52,118
The grave no more held Him than the deep held

21
00:00:52,158 --> 00:00:52,458
me.

22
00:00:53,199 --> 00:00:53,739
He rose.

23
00:00:54,599 --> 00:00:57,160
You who are sure you've fallen too far, that

24
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:58,781
is how far His mercy reaches.

25
00:00:59,421 --> 00:01:00,561
It cost Him the grave.

26
00:01:01,401 --> 00:01:03,822
Stop running, and turn: the One who went down

27
00:01:03,862 --> 00:01:05,743
into your dark and rose again is Jesus.

28
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,444
Come up out of the deep, and live.
